Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.430
OK, we have to demand that.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:12.570
Corporate media live fact check, Donald Trump's
corona virus, press briefings.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:18.670
You all may know that I've been covering the
press briefings live roughly five, six days

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.670
a week.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.090
Usually I miss one each week that Trump does.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.391
I make an effort to be as.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:29.730
Hot up as possible on all of the things Donald
Trump is likely to lie about.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.730
So that in real time I can fact check it.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:39.570
When Donald Trump says chloroquine looks really
good, I'm ready to tell you that it is one

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.920
of dozens of things being looked at.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.920
But the early trials aren't so good.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.320
And a lot of them lack the rigor that a true
randomized, controlled, peer reviewed trial

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.320
would have.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.300
Okay. Trump says chloroquine +s throw myson.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.300
Why not?

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.300
What do you have to lose?

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.820
And I make an effort to be ready with what
you might have to lose.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.520
And the side effects, chloroquine poisoning,
so on and so forth.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.080
This week, Trump shifted his zinc.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.819
Zinc does not cure coronavirus.

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:11.369
And we have to be ready to talk about that,
Trump said last week.

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:15.600
Sometimes a scarf is better than a mask at
preventing contagion.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.600
That's not true.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.260
We have to be ready with the data.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:24.289
There's been a huge debate about whether corporate
media outlets should air the Trump press briefings

00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:25.289
or not.

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:27.719
Should they skip the Trump part and go right
to the doctors?

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:31.850
Well, the problem with that is very often
in the midst of the lies, Trump is actually

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:36.280
announcing important policy during his part,
whether it's an extension of the social distancing

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.460
guidelines or whatever.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.319
Trump says no one could have predicted this.

00:01:40.319 --> 00:01:44.220
We've got to be ready to point out, actually,
a lot of people were predicting it.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:49.429
So here's my challenge to corporate media
and I encourage you to let them know.

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:55.170
And to his credit, Joe Scarborough actually
said the other day, MSNBC has to be alive.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.259
Fact checking these.

00:01:56.259 --> 00:01:59.709
They are so riddled with lies, they have to
be live, fact checked.

00:01:59.709 --> 00:02:03.530
The challenges demand that corporate media
live.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:08.810
Fact check the press briefings, put a 90 second
delay on it, 90 seconds on.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:15.050
Google is more than enough for a team of producers
to find the truth about the things Trump is

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.050
lying about.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:24.010
If by myself, I can catch half the lies, a
fully staffed multi-million 10 million hundred

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:29.690
million dollar operation has to be able to
handle the research and the graphics required

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:30.850
to live.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.860
Fact check these press press briefings.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.420
Airing them without fact checking is really
easy to do.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.920
Airing them, not airing them at all is easy
to do.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.630
It's easy to critique as well.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.630
Right.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:49.720
The the real work, the value earn, you know,
should show us that you're worth something.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.160
Is the message to corporate media is to run
them.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.770
But live fact check.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.820
And you know, for the media outlets that like
